    "report": "The contact details come back hidden after a cancellation because Booking's paid-stay query excluded cancelled bookings. I removed that filter, and the fix is committed on `main` as `ff6001a`. Nothing is pushed.\n\n**Cause:** `hasPaidStay` in `src/Contexts/Booking/Infrastructure/PostgresBookingQueries.ts` had `AND b.status <> 'cancelled'`. Messaging asks this question through `IPaidBookings` each time a conversation is read. Once the paid booking was cancelled, the answer became false and the held-back view came back. ADR 55 and the port's doc comment both say the answer holds \"whatever the booking's status now\", so the filter contradicted the documented rule.\n\n**Change:**\n- `PostgresBookingQueries.ts`: dropped the cancelled-status filter. Nothing else in the query changed.\n- `conversations.routes.e2e.spec.ts`: the existing \"hides them … then shows everything in full\" test now also cancels the paid booking and checks that the traveller and the host still see the message in full.\n\n**Verification:**\n- The conversations e2e spec passes, 15 of 15, run through `yarn test`.\n- With the fix reverted, the extended test fails, so it does catch the bug.\n- Prettier, ESLint, `yarn typecheck` and `yarn check:conventions` are all clean.\n- I did not run the full unit or e2e suites.\n\n**Choices and unclear points:**\n- You said to commit on the current branch, which is `main`. The project's git guidance says to branch first when on the default branch. I followed your explicit instruction; if you'd rather have a branch, the commit can be moved.\n- The request didn't say whether a refund should also lift the hold. I left that alone, because the ADR already says a refunded paid stay keeps lifting it, and the filter was the only thing that changed.\n- I didn't touch the \"declared paid\" path or the message-reading logic in `GetConversationQueryHandler`. I read them and they look correct.",
